            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="CDIFDataDescription.CDIFDataDescriptionPackage"/>
            <body>Data Description profile additions: variable-level physical types, primary keys, statistics, value-domain description, distribution-level physical mappings.</body>
         </ownedComment>
         <name>CDIFDataDescription</name>
         <packagedElement xmi:id="CDIFDataDescription.XsdAnyUri" xmi:uuid="https://w3id.org/cdif/data_description/1.1/xmi/#XsdAnyUri" xmi:type="uml:DataType">
            <ownedComment xmi:id="CDIFDataDescription.XsdAnyUri-ownedComment" xmi:uuid="https://w3id.org/cdif/data_description/1.1/xmi/#XsdAnyUri-ownedComment" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
               <annotatedElement xmi:idref="CDIFDataDescription.XsdAnyUri"/>
               <body>Primitive data type "anyURI" of the XML Schema data types.

Definition from XML Schema Part 2: Datatypes Second Edition: "anyURI" represents a Uniform Resource Identifier Reference (URI). An "anyURI" value can be absolute or relative, and may have an optional fragment identifier (i.e., it may be a URI Reference). This type should be used to specify the intention that the value fulfills the role of a URI as defined by [RFC 2396], as amended by [RFC 2732]. For details see https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#anyURI.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <name>XsdAnyUri</name>
         </packagedElement>
         <packagedElement xmi:id="CDIFDataDescription.Classes" xmi:uuid="https://w3id.org/cdif/data_description/1.1/xmi/#Classes-package" xmi:type="uml:Package">
